# New feature IDs, actual earlier feature IDs, and the concrete control/interpretation audit.
rows={
'32-01':('', '', 'Direct grētan farewell takes accusative ēow, with agreeing ealle. The selected prior farewell sense is grētan-take-leave, ch12; this is not a quotation of the p165 bidding construction.'),
'32-02':('', 'u12-preterite-anterior u09-perception-infinitive', 'The rowing precedes seeing; the simple preterite expresses contextual anteriority. Accusative Hǣlend is the walking actor of gān. Approximation swilce, the tens and uppan are visibly supported. Masculine sǣ agrees with the actual prior selected noun system.'),
'32-03':('u16-arisan-indicative u16-geswican-absolute', '', 'Arising, commanding and speaking are three retained events. Bebēad has dative wind recipient; Geswīc is the independently attested singular absolute command, not the abandoned gestillan model.'),
'32-04':('u16-geswican-absolute u16-weorthan-arise', '', 'The wind ceases; nominative smyltnes is the event that comes about. Wearð is lexical, with no participle. Actual prior feminine nominative miclu agrees with smyltnes.'),
'32-05':('', '', 'Dependent whence/whither contents retain present viewpoint. Ne wāst is the existing uncontracted negative sequence; no nytan paradigm is imported. Voice is accusative object of hear.'),
'32-06':('', 'u09-perception-infinitive', 'Accusative twēgen brōðor are the sending actors; their singular net is the thing sent into the sea. The plain sęndan infinitive is explicitly promoted through its complete plain/inflected pair.'),
'32-07':('u16-don-finite-result u16-aefter-follow', 'u09-dative-speaking-recipient u10-present-future', 'The command plural addresses the two men, but the controlled result subject is dual git. The finite result has nominative plural fisceras and indicative bēoð, directly evidenced by BT208. The leaving event is subsequent; nętt has zero plural. Sōna is visible support.'),
'32-08':('u16-aeswician-frame u16-aeswician-indicative u16-aceorfan-frame u16-aceorfan-indicative u16-of-particle', 'u07-passive', 'Disjunctive singular hand or foot takes singular ǣswicað; the offended person is accusative. Generic hit resumes whichever member is in view. Off is a particle. Keep ðæt before the first clause, omit it only after than; retain both conditional alternatives and the passive fire clause.'),
'32-09':('u16-forleosan-frame u16-forleosan-indicative', '', 'Hæfð, forlīest, forlǣtt, gǣð and sēcð remain distinct present actions; forwearð is past within the identifying relative. One is selected out of the set by supplied of + dative. The question keeps ne.'),
'32-10':('u16-blissian-frame u16-blissian-indicative u16-ofer-rejoicing u16-degree-comparison', 'u09-reported-statement', 'The first hit in the supplied happening clause is impersonal, the second is the sheep. Finde is present subjunctive. Swīðor compares degree of rejoicing over two accusative objects, each introduced by ofer; it is not the prior preference sense.'),
'32-11':('u16-cleopian-indicative u16-blissian-frame u16-forleosan-frame', 'u07-participle-agreement', 'Cleopað is singular summons, Blissiað plural command. Omitting have yields the actual selected first-singular fand. Attributive forloren is explicitly strong accusative neuter singular after mīn, not a free inference from its participial base.'),
'33-01':('', '', 'The supplied participial entry phrase has plural actors; finding remains finite fundon. Selected bearn is the actual earlier child word. Marian is the separately supported oblique name; mid governs dative.'),
'33-02':('', '', 'All four commands remain, with the exact final sęcge in the until clause. On niht is a visible time expression. The singular command recipient takes the child and its mother; the place remains Egypt.'),
'33-03':('u16-arisan-indicative u16-cleopian-indicative u16-gefyllan-utterance', 'u07-passive', 'The narrative has actual selected nōm and fōr. The purpose retains passive gefylled wǣre without a separate might word; the reported utterance retains its passive and its by/through agents. The embedded quotation uses first-singular cleopode without have.'),
'33-04':('u16-biddan-requested-thing', 'u11-biddan-person', 'Hwæs is the genitive thing requested. Magon is plural indicative possibility, followed by plain biddan. The old ch11 personal-asking frame does not itself teach the genitive thing; that government is new here.'),
'33-05':('', 'u07-gieman-genitive-complement', 'Actual gieman-1 has the ch07 rule-over sense, and u07-gieman-genitive-complement already teaches its genitive complement. Cook296 explicitly confirms rule over, §156f; no unnecessary wealdan system is substituted.'),
'33-06':('u16-wenan-genitive', 'u15-negative-concord', 'The actual expectation sense wenan-u15-suppose remains ch15. Its genitive object is newly taught: nāhtes and exception dēaðes selfes. The earlier u15-wenan-content feature licenses a finite content clause, not this government. Supply the complete negative/exceptive nominal phrase.'),
'33-07':('', 'u05-cessation-genitive u10-present-future', 'Actual geswican-cease and genitive cessation are prior ch05. The simple present geswīcst receives the instructed future interpretation; no new willan auxiliary or accusative work object is required.'),
'33-08':('u16-expectation-findan', '', 'The exact Wēn is ðæt pattern introduces possible finding with finde, newly taught present subjunctive. A nominal frēond is the thing found, not a genitive dependent of Wēn.'),
'33-09':('', 'u09-dative-speaking-recipient', 'Direct speech retains its own first-person singular/plural viewpoints and willan forms. The actual source phrase is on fiscnoð, explicitly supplied as an activity expression; the companion remains mid + dative.'),
'33-10':('', 'u15-negative-concord', 'Going out, going aboard and catching nothing are retained as past events. Ne and nāwiht cooperate in negation. On scip is a goal; on ðǣre niht is the separately supplied time expression.'),
'34-01':('', 'u06-imperative-negative', 'The free-choice clause is subjunctive sīe; the negative command is singular forlǣt with accusative mē. The whole command pair is now explicitly taught.'),
'34-02':('u16-indefinite-relative-fedan', '', 'Nānne is the possible person to be found; fēde is the relative provider action. Finde/fēde are present subjunctives, each backed by its complete present system. Return uses the earlier ęfthweorfan lexeme with a newly taught command pair.'),
'34-03':('', '', 'The image says books. The entire genyhtsumien clause is supplied from p167 with that noun substitution; mīna bēc is nominative plural, unc dual dative, bǣm dative plural. Do not treat the earlier mistaken hooks transcription as a source error.'),
'34-04':('', '', 'Both modifies the two boys; gelǣrede is the selected plural lexical adjective educated. The source editor teaches its adjective system; no separate full gelǣran finite conjugation is inferred from it.'),
'34-05':('', '', 'Bēgen and rihtwīse agree with the plural persons. Beforan Gode retains the previously taught relational use, rather than inventing a new clause.'),
'34-06':('u16-halsian-oath', '', 'Accusative person ðē is solemnly charged, by an accusative oath standard. The request takes ðæt with sęcge, recipient ūs dative; gif introduces the whether-content with sīe. Living-God participial inflection is supplied as an exact phrase.'),
'34-07':('', 'u09-perception-infinitive', 'One accusative actor Mannes Sunu controls both plain perception infinitives sittan/cuman. English sitting/coming describes perceived actions and does not force participles. Preserve the source-controlled right-hand accusative phrase; the cloud phrase is locative dative.'),
'34-08':('', '', 'The wish is impersonal Sīe inc, with dative dual inc and plural bǣm. Æfter incrum gelēafan is visibly supplied according-to support, not inferred from following-person æfter.'),
'34-09':('', '', 'Is tō cumanne is a newly supplied complete construction for intended/impending coming. Earlier is/cumanne morphology and the prior purpose-after-cuman feature do not license this wesan construction. The whole reward clause is also supplied. Preserve the printed erroneous āgyltan §113 hint and declare its correction to āgyldan strongIII; āgylt is valid3sg, with dative ǣlcum.'),
'34-10':('', 'u15-negative-concord', 'Temporal present cymð gives the future condition; uncontracted ne wāt and negative nān remain. Hwanon introduces the indirect question. No negative witan table or English shall auxiliary is added.'),
'34-11':('u16-cleopian-cry u16-cleopian-indicative u16-cunnan-person', '', 'Distinguish intransitive crying from teaching and speaking. Cunnan takes a personal accusative; witan here takes whence-content. Retain the direct speaker’s ic/mē and the personal source phrase of mē selfum. The sending relative has nominative sē/ðe, but the knowing relative accusative ðone.'),
'34-12':('u16-cunnan-person u16-healdan-keep', 'u10-present-future', 'The first knowing is past cūðon without have; present cann contrasts with conditional reported cunne in final position. Bēo expresses the stated future without shall and takes the dative comparison ēow. Healde now explicitly means keep/observe the accusative saying.'),
'34-13':('u16-wuldrian-frame u16-wuldrian-indicative', 'u09-reported-statement', 'Self-glorification has accusative mē selfne. Nis plus nāwiht is negative predication; the Father is the glorifying subject. The final reported sīe preserves the instructed final position. Be ðǣm is supplied concerning-support.'),
'35-01':('', '', 'The singular fōh command and accusative masculine ball phrase use the actual prior fōn imperative. Source editor separately evidences ðoðor and its complete nominal system.'),
'35-02':('', '', 'Hwā asks for the singular catching subject; fēng is preterite3sg. Blacan agrees weak accusative masculine singular with the ball after ðone.'),
'35-03':('u16-genitive-route', '', 'The commanded path is genitive ðæs weges as at169.16–17/§157. Relative ðe identifies the route already traversed; cōme is past2sg, not a present subjunctive inferred from its ending.'),
'35-04':('u16-plegian-play u16-plegian-indicative u16-don-substitute u16-adverbial-action-comparison', 'u15-negative-concord', 'Plegode denotes ordinary playing. The comparative qualifies the action; finite dyde repeats it with its own first-singular agreement. Tō-dæg stays in the current speaker’s day; no English do-support is taught.'),
'35-05':('u16-don-substitute u16-adverbial-action-comparison', 'u15-negative-concord', 'The repeated action is singing, carried by third-singular dyde. Narrated nū is retained as instructed, not automatically shifted to ðā. Ne/nǣfre gives never, and bęt qualifies the action.'),
'35-06':('', '', 'Three sufferings precede the duration statement; āne niht and ānne dæg are accusative extents. On ðissum sǣ is locative dative with the actual prior masculine sea system.'),
'35-07':('u16-witan-person u16-laedan-passive-carry', 'u07-passive', 'Wiste has an accusative personal object; lǣded is unprefixed carrying in a passive. The endpoint uses source-controlled ōð. Nān earthly man is the subject of the prohibition, with mōt plus plain sprecan, not a modern future prediction.'),
'35-08':('', '', 'The singular gate/way agreement is supplied as a bounded figurative route, not generalized to every coordination. Fēawe is a supplied plural substantive; the finding clause is indicative plural findað.'),
'35-09':('', '', 'Cumað is present plural indicative; on scēapa gegierelum is clothing, not goal or time, and receives visible support. Preserve the contrast between outward clothing and inward wolves.'),
'35-10':('', 'u07-passive', 'The first ðā is when, the second then; ðǣr supplies there. Approach takes the dative city gate; boren is passive bēran. The source hint is then ðā, not an instruction to add an intransitive gān event.'),
'35-11':('u16-iernan-frame', 'u09-perception-infinitive', 'Accusative mǣden is the running actor, iernan the plain perception infinitive; geond takes accusative strǣte. The indefinite girl needs no invented gendered pronoun.'),
'35-12':('u16-smierwan-frame', '', 'Smiere is the singular command modelled on gierwan; mē is accusative person, mid ęle the anointing material. BT smire is an evidenced spelling alternative, not silently mixed into the selected ie table.'),
'35-13':('', '', 'Sęllað is the actual prior plural command; ūs is dative recipient. Of ēowrum ęle is a visibly supplied partitive phrase; do not mislabel it as spatial departure.'),
'35-14':('u16-aliesan-indicative', 'u10-present-future', 'The finite ālīest is newly covered by the complete indicative of prior ālīesan deliver. The object ēow is plural accusative. Frige is the expressly supplied predicate plural, supported by Cook Exercises48; it is not nominative singular frēo.'),
'36-01':('u16-deman-command-before-ge', 'u06-imperative-negative', 'Teach the complete dēm/dēmað command pair and the bounded dēme immediately before gē. Unit4 explicitly excluded this shortened postposed-pronoun form. Cook55 selects it here; the second command remains dēmað. Be + appearance is supplied according-to support.'),
'36-02':('u16-bewendan-frame u16-bewendan-indicative u16-bewendan-reflexive u16-thwean-frame u16-thwean-indicative', '', 'Bewęnde has the instructed dative reflexive him. Preserve each reported act and contrast: seeing, entering, water not given, washing with tears. ðēos refers to the female person despite grammatical neuter wīf, with explicit support. Tō feet is intended-use support; ðwōh takes accusative feet and mid + liquid.'),
'36-03':('', '', 'First clause retains verb-last sealdest and no indefinite article. Prior inēode expresses entered. Supply the exact negative cessation clause with both ne, attested BT879b; it means continued kissing, not withheld kisses. Do not add a have auxiliary.'),
'36-04':('u16-smierwan-frame u16-smierwan-indicative', '', 'Second-singular smieredest requires -st; third-singular smierede does not. Plural oils is retained as instructed. Both clauses have accusative body part and mid + dative material, with consistent selected ie stems.'),
'36-05':('u16-forgiefan-forgive', 'u07-passive u07-predicate-participle-variants', 'Synna is the plural passive subject, hiere the person forgiven, and forgiefen the newly productive uninflected predicate. Therefore is not because; distinct For-ðon support is supplied. The causal clause keeps final lufode and the instructed intensity adverb.'),
'36-06':('u16-forgiefan-forgive', '', 'Supply the compressed attracted-relative sentence. First lǣs is the prompt-controlled neuter accusative degree expression; second lǣs is nominative amount forgiven. The dative relative belongs to forgiveness, not to a general dative subject rule for lufian.'),
'36-07':('', '', 'Supply the entire impersonal permission frame: hit + ālīefð, dative allowed person ðē, accusative wife hīe, and tō wīfe as a role. Omit the English is and do not bind the wife-role preposition to a destination sense.'),
'36-08':('u16-biddan-requested-thing', '', 'Supply the promise/free-choice bridge. Dative hiere is giving recipient, accusative resumptive ðæt the thing given; inside the free-choice clause hwæs is genitive requested thing and hine accusative requested person. Bǣde is preterite subjunctive; no should word is inserted.'),
'36-09':('', '', 'Supply myngod as an uninflected predicative participle with fram + dative agent. Give is the singular command Sęle with dative recipient and accusative head. The John genitive and Baptist genitive are separately evidenced by the source editor; the exact Cook headword fuluhtere is preserved.'),
'36-10':('u16-beheafdian-frame u16-beheafdian-indicative u16-asendan-absolute', '', 'The sending patient is unexpressed as in the source; the coordinated beheading has accusative Johannem, separately evidenced. The place is dative cwearterne. The active wording is not silently rewritten as a different causative command.'),
'36-11':('', '', 'Indefinite man is the stated one subject; brōhte is preterite3sg. Accusative head is brought on a dative dish. This final event is not omitted or absorbed into the prior sentence.')}
assert len(rows)==59
